From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:29:39 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] swgl gpu: colour textures live on the GPU only, CPU buffers
 on demand

With GPU shading every SWGL texture had a CPU buffer and a Direct3D copy,
and on a phone the GPU's memory is the phone's: render targets and atlases
were held twice (the Lumia 650 was killed over its 390 MB limit on
YouTube). Now an RGBA8/R8 texture SWGL allocates is born resident on the
GPU with no CPU buffer and nothing to upload, and a texture whose GPU copy
is current after a draw, clear or copy frees its CPU buffer. TexSubImage2D
into such a texture goes straight to the GPU; anything on the CPU that
needs the pixels (CPU draws, samplers, blits, ReadPixels, locks, clears)
brings the buffer back with a readback. Data textures the vertex stage
reads on the CPU (RGBA32F/I) and depth keep theirs. The log reports copies
freed and brought back and the CPU memory saved.

Reftests on a 9_3 device: 944/1018 and 895/1018 (compositor tiles) match
the CPU render, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
